    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326">

                <pb facs="0492" n="178" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg178"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-16">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">September 16, 1914</hi>.</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Please inform Foreign Office that Department has inquired of Tokyo and Peking
                    whether there was foundation for the English <pb facs="0493" n="179"
                        xml:id="pg179"/> press reports stating that Japanese Government proposes to
                    extend war to regions east of Hwang-ho River, to expel all Germans not only from
                    Dalny but from Mukden, Changchun and even Tientsin, and has received replies
                    stating that reports are entirely unfounded and untrue.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
